#: freeports_dev.ci.metrics.Metric:3 of
msgid ""
"``pattern`` is the name as a shell glob, so that the per-package families"
" -- which cannot be enumerated, since the set of packages is whatever the"
" repository holds -- are matched rather than listed. A metric with no "
"wildcard matches only itself."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.metrics.Metric.is_family:1 of
msgid ""
"True when the name carries a wildcard, i.e. it names a family and not one"
" figure."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.metrics.REGISTRY:3 of
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The baselines this table was seeded from were measured, never wished for:"
" the pipeline that preceded this one asked for 90 % of a documentation "
"figure that read 25.93 %, which is how a threshold nobody can clear ends "
"up being the threshold everybody disables."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.metrics.SLOW:1 of
msgid ""
"Measured by ``make ci`` and read from the last one at commit time. "
"Minutes, not seconds."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.metrics.env_name:3 of
msgid ""
"The metric upper-cased, dots and dashes as underscores, prefixed "
"``FREEPORTS_CI_MIN_`` -- mechanical, so that a person who knows the "
"metric knows the variable without a lookup table."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.metrics.find:3 of
msgid ""
"Exact names are tried before families, so that ``docs.python`` is itself "
"and not an oddly spelled member of ``docs.python.*``. Without that order "
"the aggregate and the per-package family would fight over the same "
"string, and which one won would depend on table order."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.metrics.known_in:3 of
msgid ""
"This is what makes a threshold on a metric the repository cannot measure "
"a *configuration error* rather than a silent no-op: a formats repository "
"naming ``tests.rust.lines`` has written down a demand nothing will ever "
"evaluate, and a threshold that can never be evaluated is a threshold "
"somebody thinks they have."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.metrics.split_package_key:3 of
msgid ""
"The aggregate a per-package key overrides is the same name with the "
"package taken out, which is what lets the gate remove a specifically "
"named package from the aggregate's denominator without a second table "
"saying which aggregate each family belongs to."
msgstr ""

